! Right Alt (keycode 108) is the Hangul toggle for fcitx5 (TriggerKeys=Hangul).
! It must also be bound to NO modifier -- if it stays in mod1 it still behaves
! as Alt and swallows every keystroke typed while it is held.
!
! Left Alt (keycode 64, next to space) and the small outer key (keycode 133)
! are swapped: the key next to space is Super ($mod in i3, Mac-Cmd-like), the
! outer one is Alt.
!
! mod1/mod4 are rebuilt from scratch rather than using `remove`:
!   - `remove` matches by keysym, so once a keycode line below has taken
!     effect it silently stops matching, leaving the key bound to the old
!     modifier -- broken, yet containing nothing to grep for.
!   - once no key carries a keysym at all, `remove` is a hard error that
!     aborts the rest of this file.
! `clear` + `add` of keysyms that always exist is order-independent and cannot
! fail.
keycode 108 = Hangul
keycode  64 = Super_L
keycode 133 = Alt_L Meta_L
clear mod1
clear mod4
add mod1 = Alt_L Meta_L
add mod4 = Super_L Super_R Hyper_L
